I wrote the session plan: two task files and the issue responses in session_plan/. The commit step didn't take: .gitignore lists session_plan/, so git add refused. I didn't force-add it, since the planned command already tolerates failure (|| true). The files are on disk for the next phase, but they're in no commit, so a fresh checkout won't have them.

• **task_01.md, #993 (product, my own find):** when yoyo -p is interrupted with Ctrl+C, it currently exits 0 and prints the REPL's "press Ctrl+C again" hint into stdout.
  • **Fix:** in single-prompt mode, send a short note to stderr and exit 130 (the usual Ctrl+C exit code). Text already streamed stays on stdout, and the interactive REPL behaves exactly as before.
  • **Mode check:** the fix should key on single-prompt mode, not on whether stdout is a terminal, because -p into a terminal also exits after one turn.
  • Tests: pinned in tests/print_stdout_contract.rs. The signal is sent only after the first streamed bytes arrive, to avoid timing flakes. A positive control proves the test actually fails when the fix is reverted.
• **task_02.md, #994 (product, filed by the creator):** crates.io installs print "dev" in --version.
  • **Fix:** `build.rs` reads the published commit from `.cargo_vcs_info.json`, which `cargo publish` writes into the package, and only falls back to `git rev-parse when that file is absent. With no hash at all, version_line()` prints just the date, never "dev". Local builds stay exactly as they are now.
  • **Staleness probe:** the assessment suspects local builds can show an old commit hash, because `build.rs` only re-runs when `DAY_COUNT` changes. That's unverified, so the first step checks it before anything in build.rs is edited. If it reproduces, it gets its own issue rather than a fix in this task.
• Issue responses: #988 and #982 are deferred with reasons, and nothing is owed on #991.

